WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:05.680
<i>Christmas is over, but it's not quiet New Years' yet.</i>

00:06.680 --> 00:08.800
<i>And I have a day off after a long while.</i>

00:09.390 --> 00:13.310
The president himself is here to personally introduce this chapel.

00:13.090 --> 00:14.970
Usami Group, President Usami Fuyuhiko

00:13.540 --> 00:14.730
Welcome.

00:15.150 --> 00:16.750
Usagi's father!!

00:16.790 --> 00:20.150
But before that, your son, the managing director of the company,

00:20.150 --> 00:24.880
was the architect behind that fresh, innovative design of the Aoyama aquarium, correct?

00:25.270 --> 00:26.030
Yes.

00:26.100 --> 00:29.400
He'll be celebrating his wedding ceremony very soon in this chapel.

00:29.720 --> 00:34.050
<i>Son? Usagi's brother marrying!? No way! Seriously!?</i>

00:34.240 --> 00:35.500
<i>But he...</i>

00:36.030 --> 00:37.380
I love you.

00:38.230 --> 00:39.980
<i>...persistently kept saying that!</i>

00:40.700 --> 00:42.050
<i>Hurray!</i>

00:43.020 --> 00:46.930
<i>I see, I see, I see!! Oh, Oh! I'm thrilled!!</i>

00:47.120 --> 00:49.660
<i>Many congratulations on your wedding ceremony!!</i>

00:49.660 --> 00:51.830
Misaki, what are you doing?

00:51.880 --> 00:53.180
Oh, good morning!

00:55.190 --> 00:57.620
<i>Oh, shoot! I can't let him see this!</i>

00:58.180 --> 01:02.140
I said no! Don't come! You're pestering me! It's annoying!

01:02.950 --> 01:04.600
Usagi-san, what's the matter?

01:06.060 --> 01:09.940
I'll keep pestering! No matter how many times you deny, I <i>will</i> have you marry me!

01:09.980 --> 01:14.950
Marriage is made in heaven

01:15.280 --> 01:20.530
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:15.280 --> 01:20.530
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:18.230 --> 01:31.500
Junjou Romantica 2

01:20.530 --> 01:24.000
ima futari no story

01:20.530 --> 01:24.000
Now, our story...

01:25.290 --> 01:32.780
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:25.290 --> 01:32.780
Our future is going to shine on.

01:36.220 --> 01:41.510
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:36.220 --> 01:41.510
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:41.980 --> 01:46.340
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:41.980 --> 01:46.340
and always lose my nerve.

01:46.340 --> 01:51.940
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:46.340 --> 01:51.940
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

01:51.940 --> 01:55.570
kimi to aeru nara

01:51.940 --> 01:55.570
if it means I can see you.

01:57.600 --> 02:02.580
ame ni utarete furueru koe

01:57.600 --> 02:02.580
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

02:02.910 --> 02:08.180
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

02:02.910 --> 02:08.180
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

02:08.860 --> 02:11.660
boku wa yuku yo

02:08.860 --> 02:11.660
I'll go,

02:11.660 --> 02:18.410
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

02:11.660 --> 02:18.410
Until the day when I can see you.

02:19.230 --> 02:24.420
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:19.230 --> 02:24.420
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:24.420 --> 02:28.130
ima futari no story

02:24.420 --> 02:28.130
Now, our story

02:28.290 --> 02:29.940
ugokidashita

02:28.290 --> 02:29.940
has started.

02:29.940 --> 02:34.930
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:29.940 --> 02:34.930
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:34.930 --> 02:42.120
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:34.930 --> 02:42.120
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

02:45.370 --> 02:48.160
I dislike complicated affairs.

02:48.590 --> 02:51.820
That's why, I'll have you marry me.

02:52.240 --> 02:53.210
I refuse.

02:53.770 --> 02:56.590
Let me remind you that <i>I'm</i> the victim here.

02:56.950 --> 03:00.360
Do you not intend to co-operate with me even in the slightest in the biggest crisis of my life?

03:00.510 --> 03:03.600
No I don't. Deal with your problems by <i>yourself</i>.

03:03.840 --> 03:05.150
Don't drag others in it.

03:06.080 --> 03:08.430
Oh come on! You're single anyway!

03:08.640 --> 03:11.590
Unfortunate for you, but I have Misaki.

03:11.990 --> 03:12.830
He and I are-

03:16.000 --> 03:18.480
You're taking the joke a bit too far, Sensei!

03:18.720 --> 03:20.950
What the hell're you sayin'!? I'll kill you!!

03:21.280 --> 03:23.730
You're... not a servant?

03:24.450 --> 03:27.260
Eh? Ahh, I'm just a freeloader.

03:27.470 --> 03:28.630
Special skills?

03:28.730 --> 03:30.350
No skills in particular.

03:30.470 --> 03:31.240
Hobbies?

03:31.330 --> 03:34.140
Um, let's see. I'm pretty hooked to manga right now.

03:34.960 --> 03:36.280
You're a boring person, huh.

03:36.460 --> 03:37.450
Boring
person

03:37.710 --> 03:39.810
Kaoruko, cut it out.

03:39.920 --> 03:44.360
Even boring people, in a boring way, have many things about them that aren't so boring.

03:44.440 --> 03:46.110
Well excuse me for being boring!!

03:46.110 --> 03:49.090
And anyway, why do you have say it like that!?

03:49.360 --> 03:50.540
Who is she!?

03:51.200 --> 03:52.290
My cousin.

03:51.200 --> 03:52.290
His cousin.

03:53.440 --> 03:53.900
<i>What?</i>

03:54.980 --> 03:55.840
His cousin?

03:57.690 --> 04:00.200
I was told that my parents were gravely ill.

04:00.300 --> 04:04.120
So I rushed back from England only to find out that it was all a big lie.

04:04.600 --> 04:09.010
Uncle Fuyuhiko is scheming with my parents to marry me to Haruhiko-san.

04:09.360 --> 04:12.350
Haru-, meaning, Usagi-san's elder brother?

04:13.220 --> 04:15.900
Hm? You know Haruhiko-san?

04:16.540 --> 04:18.380
Uh, yeah, sort of.

04:18.820 --> 04:20.570
I mean, he was on TV just recently.

04:20.970 --> 04:21.710
On TV?

04:21.960 --> 04:26.470
Oh, your father was promoting the new chapel they opened up,

04:26.560 --> 04:29.100
and said that your brother would get married there.

04:29.610 --> 04:30.790
Promoting!?

04:30.900 --> 04:33.520
What's up with that!? I can't believe this!!

04:33.940 --> 04:36.070
Akihiko-niisama, please!

04:36.810 --> 04:41.260
If I were to be with you, Haruhiko-san's natural enemy, nobody could meddle with my life.

04:41.430 --> 04:42.940
You just have to pretend!

04:43.080 --> 04:44.020
Go home.

04:44.440 --> 04:46.920
Even if it was just a pretense, I wouldn't do it.

04:47.290 --> 04:49.620
If you want a sham wedding, look for someone else.

04:53.160 --> 04:54.970
Usagi-san, um...

04:55.420 --> 04:58.250
Even if it's just for a little bit, why don't you let her stay here?

04:58.760 --> 05:00.400
Are you okay with that?

05:00.820 --> 05:02.450
Well, don't you feel sorry about her?

05:07.100 --> 05:10.450
Nii-sama, I'm not asking you to let me stay for free.

05:10.450 --> 05:11.910
If it's money, I don't wan't it.

05:12.010 --> 05:13.910
Then, how about bears?

05:14.220 --> 05:17.760
Too bad. I already have all of those.

05:17.810 --> 05:19.760
You can have all of these right now as a bonus.

05:20.000 --> 05:21.990
If you think you can tempt me, it's useless.

05:22.060 --> 05:23.990
Plus these as an extra bonus!

05:24.070 --> 05:25.950
Is that the best you can do to tempt me?

05:26.090 --> 05:29.010
Plus this on top of all those too, right now!

05:29.370 --> 05:31.760
I can't do anything for you, but please make yourself at home.

05:32.370 --> 05:33.120
<i>Huh?</i>

05:33.600 --> 05:36.340
I'm begging you. Please don't take any more bears than these.

05:36.950 --> 05:38.870
I'll do something about Kaoruko.

05:39.220 --> 05:41.520
Yeah. It's really unreasonable, isn't it?

05:41.800 --> 05:43.520
They are blood relatives even.

05:43.710 --> 05:46.350
He and Kaoruko aren't blood relatives.

05:47.350 --> 05:49.650
Kaoruko is from my mother's side of the family,

05:50.220 --> 05:52.070
my father was adopted,

05:52.240 --> 05:54.110
and my brother and I have different mothers.

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Husband

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi's
Mother's
sister

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi's
Mother

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi's
Father

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi's
Brother's
Mother

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Kaoruko

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi-san

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Usagi's brother

05:53.590 --> 05:57.590
Like this?

05:54.360 --> 05:56.500
In other words, they both are complete strangers.

05:58.270 --> 06:01.770
Anyway, avoiding that family altogether would be the best defense.

06:02.340 --> 06:04.080
Yeah, that might be right.

06:04.200 --> 06:05.550
Well, be careful.

06:05.550 --> 06:06.420
Misaki.

06:07.410 --> 06:08.660
I'm saying this for you.

06:09.060 --> 06:09.550
Huh?

06:10.520 --> 06:13.100
Until this whole thing settles down, don't go outside.

06:13.590 --> 06:15.440
Luckily, your school's on break too.

06:15.850 --> 06:17.540
Don't say something ridiculous.

06:17.540 --> 06:19.200
And just what do I do about my part time job?

06:20.170 --> 06:21.940
There's no need for you to have a job.

06:22.390 --> 06:23.720
It'll be okay.

06:23.870 --> 06:25.190
I'm not a kid, you know.

06:25.420 --> 06:27.470
You're "okay" isn't reliable at all.

06:28.110 --> 06:29.490
I told you things will be fine!

06:29.600 --> 06:32.360
You say you love me, then why do you doubt me?

06:32.960 --> 06:36.150
Usagi-san, have a little faith in me!

06:40.820 --> 06:43.220
I do... have faith in you.

06:43.910 --> 06:45.650
Then everything's fine.

06:48.560 --> 06:49.730
Where's Nii-sama?

06:50.470 --> 06:52.480
Oh, he's gone out for buying cigarettes.

07:02.380 --> 07:04.480
Oh, I'll make some tea.

07:05.520 --> 07:08.560
Nobody cares one bit about me.

07:09.040 --> 07:10.800
What? That can't be.

07:10.800 --> 07:14.570
I don't know how Uncle Fuyuhiko managed to wheedle my parents into this,

07:14.810 --> 07:17.840
but it means he decided that doing so would benefit the company.

07:19.470 --> 07:20.600
It's always like that.

07:21.360 --> 07:23.460
My parents just decide everything as they wish.

07:24.240 --> 07:26.260
They don't even let me do the things that I want to,

07:26.760 --> 07:29.290
dismissing everything by saying that it's my selfishness.

07:30.260 --> 07:33.040
If you have something you want to do, why not just do it?

07:35.110 --> 07:37.870
I just said that everyone's against it, didn't I!?

07:38.600 --> 07:43.150
Ah... but, you alone can accomplish something you want to.

07:44.730 --> 07:48.430
That's the first time... someone said that to me.

07:50.320 --> 07:54.130
I... actually want to be a patissier.

07:54.910 --> 07:55.680
Patissier?

07:55.900 --> 07:57.930
Uh! Don't laugh, okay?

07:57.930 --> 07:59.430
I won't!

07:59.860 --> 08:01.870
I baked a cake just the other day too.

08:02.100 --> 08:02.670
Wanna see?

08:05.900 --> 08:06.400
This.

08:08.640 --> 08:10.810
D-Don't just touch me so casually!

08:11.010 --> 08:12.810
O-Ohh, sorry, sorry!

08:14.150 --> 08:14.670
Yes!

08:15.530 --> 08:16.670
It's been a while.

08:17.200 --> 08:18.380
<i>The elder Usagi!!</i>

08:18.580 --> 08:21.690
Wh-What is it? Why might you have come all this way for?

08:21.910 --> 08:23.800
I heard that Kaoruko was here.

08:23.920 --> 08:26.340
Huh? Who might that be?

08:26.740 --> 08:32.680
<i>This is bad. Kaoruko-san aside, I must not let Usagi-san bump into him at all costs!</i>

08:33.840 --> 08:35.120
The elder Usagi's here!

08:35.120 --> 08:36.010
No way!!

08:36.120 --> 08:40.700
At any rate, I'll take him out somewhere and act as if I don't know anything about you.

08:41.440 --> 08:43.440
But, what should I tell Nii-sama?

08:43.930 --> 08:45.440
Tell him I'll keep my promise.

08:45.950 --> 08:48.560
I'll definitely come back in 3 hours.

08:54.340 --> 08:55.180
So?

08:56.280 --> 08:59.350
If Kaoruko's not at home, then where is she?

08:59.520 --> 09:05.720
Hmm... let's see... for now, can we go down this road for a bit... or something?

09:08.170 --> 09:09.330
Yes, let's.

09:09.390 --> 09:13.760
I, too, for now, just need to show as if I'm searching for her.

09:14.340 --> 09:14.930
Eh?

09:15.910 --> 09:16.800
Sorry.

09:17.630 --> 09:20.470
All the mess this time is my father's doing.

09:21.470 --> 09:23.930
But why do something like this?

09:24.790 --> 09:27.500
To make me break up with you.

09:27.990 --> 09:29.610
Ohh, I see.

09:29.980 --> 09:34.040
By marrying them to someone else, the two can be torn apart forcefully-

09:34.040 --> 09:37.200
Hey, what the hell!!? What was that!!? Something's fundamentally wrong here!

09:37.220 --> 09:40.660
Looks like my father knows that I'm in love with you.

09:40.890 --> 09:43.370
Why am <i>I</i> the reason of this?

09:43.920 --> 09:47.030
Don't worry. I'll settle this once and for all.

09:47.360 --> 09:50.250
Up till now, I've listened to everything that he said,

09:50.460 --> 09:52.770
but I have no intention of obeying him this time.

09:53.190 --> 09:56.570
Please. Please clear any bizzare misunderstanding he has.

09:57.610 --> 10:00.060
Do you hate me that much?

10:00.580 --> 10:01.200
Huh?

10:01.460 --> 10:04.000
Uh, no, I didn't mean it that way...

10:04.400 --> 10:10.120
I wonder what should I do to make someone like me.

10:10.670 --> 10:11.260
Eh?

10:11.580 --> 10:15.360
I am the child of father's lover, and have a different mother than Akihiko's.

10:15.960 --> 10:17.530
You know that, don't you?

10:18.000 --> 10:19.620
Ahh... I bit...

10:20.660 --> 10:26.970
My father took me in, but even as a child, I knew where I stood.

10:28.270 --> 10:33.810
That's why, in order to be liked by everyone, I lived up to everybody's expectations perfectly.

10:34.040 --> 10:40.160
And yet, I wonder why... I found myself feeling like I was about to suffocate.

10:41.160 --> 10:44.440
Akihiko was the complete opposite of me.

10:45.890 --> 10:47.720
Nobody could sway him.

10:47.930 --> 10:50.990
He immersed himself in doing only the things he liked.

10:52.110 --> 10:55.040
And it looked like he was very happy.

10:55.500 --> 10:56.480
But,

10:57.880 --> 11:00.800
<i>But, even Usagi-san too...</i>

11:02.200 --> 11:08.050
That's why, if I stole you from Akihiko, I thought that maybe I would become happy too.

11:08.330 --> 11:10.260
<i>Hm? Somehow...</i>

11:11.100 --> 11:14.700
<i>He seems different from the impression I had of him till now.</i>

11:16.020 --> 11:16.490
<i>Oh!</i>

11:17.050 --> 11:21.240
I believe I never said anything before, no matter who stole you away.

11:22.080 --> 11:24.530
<i>Huh? But that means...</i>

11:25.360 --> 11:30.610
Haruhiko-san, aren't you just envious of Usagi-san?

11:30.840 --> 11:31.290
Hm?

11:31.640 --> 11:33.050
Oh... I mean...

11:33.300 --> 11:40.030
From what you just said, it seems that you are on bad terms with him not because you hate him,

11:40.670 --> 11:44.430
but rather you probably want to be like him, is what I thought.

11:44.810 --> 11:47.260
That means you like him, isn't it?

11:49.640 --> 11:52.260
That's the first time I heard anyone word it that way.

11:52.260 --> 11:54.260
Ah, is that so.

11:54.360 --> 11:57.700
Sorry. I just interpreted it the way I wanted.

11:59.100 --> 12:00.020
Excuse me.

12:01.950 --> 12:02.570
Yes.

12:04.510 --> 12:05.420
I understand.

12:07.420 --> 12:10.510
It was from my father, asking me to return to office immediately.

12:11.090 --> 12:13.290
Oh. Then I'll get down here.

12:13.790 --> 12:15.810
Please relay this to Kaoruko.

12:16.240 --> 12:19.340
I have no intention of marrying her.

12:19.820 --> 12:21.150
Oh. Okay.

12:21.420 --> 12:26.480
Speaking of whom, Kaoruko-san said the other day that she actually wants to be a patissier.

12:27.020 --> 12:29.860
Patissier? I see.

12:31.220 --> 12:32.700
Tokyo Station is...

12:32.850 --> 12:33.440
Sorry?

12:34.040 --> 12:36.360
one of my favourite architectural structures.

12:37.630 --> 12:41.070
I actually would have liked to become an architect.

12:41.950 --> 12:44.030
Would have liked to?

12:45.050 --> 12:46.350
Did you give up on that?

12:47.570 --> 12:50.730
My duty is to take over as head of the Usami group.

12:51.060 --> 12:56.570
Eh? Even though you can design beautiful things like that aquarium? It's such a waste...

12:57.770 --> 12:58.400
Oh!

12:59.080 --> 13:00.440
S-Sorry.

13:00.850 --> 13:04.010
I just said something really irresponsible, didn't I?

13:04.290 --> 13:05.180
You...

13:05.760 --> 13:06.220
Yes?

13:07.460 --> 13:09.130
You're a weird boy.

13:15.140 --> 13:18.490
<i>I ended up getting called weird but a weird person.</i>

13:19.310 --> 13:23.790
<i>But, Haruhiko-san didn't seem to be that bad a person as I thought he was.</i>

13:24.840 --> 13:28.130
<i>Everyone's so amazing. Each having their own dreams.</i>

13:29.570 --> 13:32.910
<i>Me... What do </i>I<i> want to become?</i>

13:34.210 --> 13:36.820
<i>I wonder, what I am good at?</i>

13:38.650 --> 13:39.080
Hm?

13:39.330 --> 13:40.580
Hello.

13:52.050 --> 13:54.860
<i>U-Usagi father!!</i>

13:55.250 --> 13:56.860
Wh-Wh? Huh?

13:57.090 --> 13:59.160
Just now, Haruhiko-san got a phone call...

13:59.320 --> 14:01.070
Ah, everything's fine.

14:01.170 --> 14:04.860
Anyway, the other day I had gone to Hokkaido on a business trip.

14:05.420 --> 14:10.180
There I got a new wood bear carving phone strap. I thought, I just have to give one to you.

14:10.590 --> 14:12.570
I-It's huge, isn't it?

14:12.720 --> 14:16.520
Here's one for Akihiko and one for Kaoruko.

14:18.180 --> 14:19.150
What's the matter?

14:19.780 --> 14:25.820
U-Um, it seems I'm being used as a reason for doing all kinds of things. It's troublesome.

14:26.260 --> 14:29.140
To begin with, this is none my business.

14:29.380 --> 14:33.690
Hmm... Except you see, that's not quite true.

14:34.370 --> 14:39.610
At any rate, I've lived longer than you and so have seen a lot more things.

14:40.360 --> 14:44.830
And for better or for worse, I have something called "social position".

14:45.420 --> 14:47.970
And there are many more things that I simply must protect.

14:48.770 --> 14:54.900
For example, my children... Yes... For me, my children are very precious.

14:55.400 --> 15:01.450
And to protect them... you're quite a troublesome existence, you see.

15:01.930 --> 15:02.530
<i>Eh?</i>

15:06.280 --> 15:09.200
Um, I'm sorry. I don't understand...

15:09.720 --> 15:13.120
You may not understand it now, but you will eventually.

15:13.450 --> 15:15.440
So then. Later.

15:19.260 --> 15:19.880
<i>Oh.</i>

15:22.430 --> 15:26.720
<i>Hurry... I must hurry back home...</i>

15:29.290 --> 15:30.900
<i>I must hurry home.</i>

15:32.030 --> 15:35.180
<i>Because I promised... that I'd be back in 3 hours.</i>

15:36.600 --> 15:39.280
<i>I must hurry back and meet him.</i>

15:41.280 --> 15:42.500
<i>Meet Usagi-san.</i>

15:45.600 --> 15:47.550
Ah! So-Sorry!

15:47.980 --> 15:50.830
Ah, Usagi-san! Why?

15:51.000 --> 15:53.440
I was just about to go search for you.

15:53.440 --> 15:53.980
Eh?

15:54.700 --> 15:56.250
I kept my promise.

15:56.910 --> 15:59.620
I waited for 3 whole hours.

16:00.380 --> 16:02.420
Because I trust you, you know.

16:03.530 --> 16:05.710
<i>I was genuinely happy,</i>

16:06.080 --> 16:09.870
O-Oh! That's amazing! Impressive! Impressive!

16:10.010 --> 16:15.220
<i>that Usagi-san trusted me and that he was worried for me.</i>

16:15.770 --> 16:21.900
Keep being this way always. If you do, it'll make things a bit easier for me too.

16:23.080 --> 16:27.250
But, right now, Usagi-san's father's words,

16:28.140 --> 16:29.210
Misaki?

16:29.500 --> 16:34.450
<i>are going round and round in my head and though I'm still shocked, I'm happy too.</i>

16:35.770 --> 16:36.740
What happened?

16:37.280 --> 16:40.180
Your face looks as if you'll cry any moment.

16:41.080 --> 16:42.980
U-Uh, i-is that so!?

16:43.450 --> 16:45.880
I don't think that's true thought.

16:46.280 --> 16:49.900
Oh, looks like Kaoruko-san's problem will be over.

16:50.300 --> 16:53.340
Haruhiko-san, too, said that he has no intention of marrying.

16:53.620 --> 16:58.280
I see. Sorry about this. You ended up getting caught up in this.

16:58.660 --> 16:59.920
Oh no! It's okay.

17:00.600 --> 17:03.080
Rather, it's good that things got sorted out.

17:03.560 --> 17:05.500
But that face doesn't look fine.

17:05.880 --> 17:07.500
What are you saying?

17:08.280 --> 17:08.980
<i>Not good.</i>

17:09.300 --> 17:11.130
I'm fine!

17:12.280 --> 17:15.440
<i>Usagi-san immediately sees through my lies.</i>

17:15.700 --> 17:17.240
<i>I can't let him know.</i>

17:18.180 --> 17:21.090
<i>Absolutely... only Usagi-san can't....</i>

17:25.160 --> 17:27.250
Any funny move and I'll kill you.

17:28.610 --> 17:32.450
<i>This is no good. I don't really want to talk to Usagi-san right now.</i>

17:34.160 --> 17:35.170
Misaki.

17:35.860 --> 17:37.240
W-What?

17:38.280 --> 17:40.000
If there's anything, just say it.

17:40.690 --> 17:42.810
I said, there's nothing.

17:43.650 --> 17:45.810
I'm going to sleep. Good night.

17:46.000 --> 17:46.980
Misaki.

17:52.380 --> 17:54.970
Do you really not trust me that much?

17:55.760 --> 17:57.090
That's not it.

17:57.680 --> 17:59.810
<i>It's not that I don't trust him.</i>

18:03.200 --> 18:04.220
<i>Just that...</i>

18:05.600 --> 18:07.160
You're quite a troublesome...

18:08.300 --> 18:14.120
While I was waiting for you, I trusted you, but worried about you at the same time.

18:14.800 --> 18:17.620
I get jealous of everything that comes near you.

18:19.820 --> 18:25.970
Please speak up. If not, I keep thinking that my existence is probably not needed and I'm pained by it.

18:26.720 --> 18:28.260
Because I worry about you.

18:29.080 --> 18:30.260
Because I love you.

18:31.960 --> 18:33.610
<i>You're mistaken Usagi-san.</i>

18:34.040 --> 18:36.960
<i>It's not like that, it's not like that.</i>

18:37.290 --> 18:38.530
<i>You know, I...</i>

18:39.250 --> 18:40.530
I want to know.

18:44.530 --> 18:48.570
<i>...won't say anything exactly because you are important to me.</i>

18:57.700 --> 19:03.690
You are quite a
troublesome
existence, you see.

18:58.140 --> 19:03.020
<i>Is that because I'm just a college student? An ordinary guy? </i>

19:03.820 --> 19:05.020
<i>Because it's me?</i>

19:07.020 --> 19:12.280
<i>To hurt Usagi-san, cause him trouble. No matter what, I can't let that happen.</i>

19:14.420 --> 19:19.650
<i>For Usagi-san to say something like that, surely must be because I had an aura of confusion around me.</i>

19:20.280 --> 19:21.450
<i>I must hide it.</i>

19:22.920 --> 19:27.520
<i>If I can't absolutely let him find out, I won't be able to stay with him.</i>

19:29.970 --> 19:31.050
<i>It's alright.</i>

19:31.800 --> 19:35.650
<i>I'm... already used to such words, aren't I?</i>

19:38.900 --> 19:43.420
Kaoruko. Your problem's over, isn't it? Hurry up and go away.

19:44.000 --> 19:47.050
What's this Nii-sama? Am I that much in your way?

19:47.280 --> 19:48.010
You're in the way.

19:48.560 --> 19:49.720
What was that!!?

19:49.840 --> 19:51.340
Ah, there, there!

19:53.930 --> 19:54.570
Yes?

19:54.640 --> 19:55.220
It's me.

19:56.410 --> 19:58.620
U-Uh, W-Wait just a second!

20:00.600 --> 20:02.280
Uh, yes.

20:02.660 --> 20:06.250
This is the first time I met someone who told me what you said the other day.

20:06.970 --> 20:11.700
Just like you said, for a brief moment, I <i>did </i>think that I like Akihiko.

20:12.560 --> 20:14.610
But that was undoubtedly not the case.

20:15.410 --> 20:16.970
I love you.

20:20.060 --> 20:22.140
Hey, what the hell!? I was talking!

20:22.140 --> 20:23.140
With whom?

20:23.680 --> 20:25.940
W-Whoever is fine, right?

20:26.250 --> 20:29.840
Oh ho! I don't like that attitude, even though you're just Misaki.

20:29.840 --> 20:32.960
If it's going to be like this, why don't I force you to spit out things?

20:33.090 --> 20:37.000
If it's going to be like this, I decided that I won't speak up, no matter what.

20:37.290 --> 20:38.700
Nii-sama.

20:39.170 --> 20:43.340
I won't go back home just yet. Because I need to speak with Misaki.

20:43.720 --> 20:44.250
What?

20:44.330 --> 20:45.410
Eh? Me?

20:45.770 --> 20:51.170
The cake you showed me the other time, I was thinking if I can try making it once?

20:51.800 --> 20:54.340
Oh, but that's really a chore.

20:54.340 --> 20:56.970
I know I can make it, that's why I'm saying it, aren't I?

20:57.290 --> 21:03.570
I-I only do things I like with the people I like, you know! Be grateful!

21:05.120 --> 21:07.480
Kaoruko-san likes me?

21:08.370 --> 21:13.530
She and I have similar taste. That's why I wanted her out of this house.

21:14.220 --> 21:15.600
<i>Amazing...</i>

21:15.800 --> 21:19.380
<i>I was confessed to by a girl for the first time in my life.</i>

21:19.620 --> 21:21.860
<i>For the first time, it was someone who isn't a guy!</i>

21:22.460 --> 21:25.250
How's that Usagi-san? I'm popular too, you know!!

21:25.560 --> 21:28.130
Stop with the boring boasting.

21:28.520 --> 21:32.570
All you need is to shut up and be loved by me alone.

21:33.050 --> 21:34.450
HUH!?

21:34.450 --> 21:36.450
What the hell!? Who do you think you are!?

21:36.200 --> 21:39.800
Nii-chan, it's spring time for me too.<i></i>

21:36.450 --> 21:37.340
I'm Usami-sama.

21:37.340 --> 21:39.960
I, too, can get a girl or two, you know!!

21:50.840 --> 21:55.980
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:50.840 --> 21:55.980
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:56.110 --> 22:01.370
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:56.110 --> 22:01.370
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

22:01.720 --> 22:06.740
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

22:01.720 --> 22:06.740
You doubled all my happiness,

22:06.740 --> 22:13.430
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

22:06.740 --> 22:13.430
and halved all my sadness.

22:13.540 --> 22:18.540
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:13.540 --> 22:18.540
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:18.940 --> 22:23.220
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:18.940 --> 22:23.220
will surely lead to you.

22:23.220 --> 22:25.980
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:23.220 --> 22:25.980
You're there up ahead of me,

22:25.980 --> 22:28.840
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:25.980 --> 22:28.840
I'm there ahead of you,

22:28.840 --> 22:34.110
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:28.840 --> 22:34.110
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:34.110 --> 22:40.010
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:34.110 --> 22:40.010
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:40.600 --> 22:45.080
mou doko he mo ikanaide

22:40.600 --> 22:45.080
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:45.080 --> 22:50.540
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:45.080 --> 22:50.540
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:50.540 --> 22:55.930
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:50.540 --> 22:55.930
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:55.930 --> 23:01.750
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:55.930 --> 23:01.750
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

23:02.140 --> 23:07.430
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

23:02.140 --> 23:07.430
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

23:17.570 --> 23:22.100
Please excuse the abrupt question, but could I know Kaoruko-san's full name?

23:22.360 --> 23:23.940
Usami Kaoruko.

23:24.140 --> 23:26.290
<i>Another Usami!!</i>

23:24.140 --> 23:31.620
Usami family specific pheromones a.k.a. Usa-mones, in action!!

23:27.460 --> 23:32.620
<i>Nii-chan, what should I do to be popular among people outside the Usami family?</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:44.940
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
Timing, Typesetting, Minor script editing and Encoding: asckj1

23:57.010 --> 24:00.000
Hate the sin but love the sinner
